.TH FERROR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
ferror \- test a Crunch stream's error indicator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int ferror(struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR ferror ()
tests the stream's error indicator without changing it.
The indicator is set by an unsuccessful stream read or write and remains set
until
.BR clearerr (3crunch)
or
.BR rewind (3crunch)
is called, or the stream is closed. A successful
.BR fseek (3crunch)
does not clear it.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns nonzero if the indicator is set and zero otherwise.
For a null stream, returns \-1 and sets
.B errno
to
.BR EINVAL ;
null is not a valid C stream argument.
Valid calls leave
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH NOTES
Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clearerr (3crunch),
.BR feof (3crunch),
.BR fread (3crunch),
.BR fwrite (3crunch),
.BR fseek (3crunch)
